{
    "category": "pde_inline_ic_param_override",
    "version": "1.0",
    "description": "Cross-binding conformance for esm-spec \u00a76.6.5 'Build-time evaluation scope': every reference resolved BEFORE the simulation runs \u2014 a coordinate-expression `ic` (\u00a711.4.1) and an inline analytic assertion `reference` \u2014 binds the model's parameters to their `parameter_overrides`-or-default values, with the overrides keyed by LOCAL parameter name (\u00a76.6). Parameter `A` (default 1.0) appears ONLY inside `ic(u)` and inside assertion references, never in an equation, so a test that overrides `A` can change the answer through the build-time scope and nowhere else. State `v` is seeded by the parameter-FREE `ic(v) = cos(pi x)` and is the independent anchor the parameter-dependent `reference` is measured against, so a binding that ignored the override in BOTH the ic and the reference cannot have the two errors cancel and still pass. Julia's tree-walk build previously resolved `parameter_overrides` by EXACT key against the flattening-qualified parameter name (`M.A`), so the spec-spelled local key (`A`) missed: the run silently used the default and the inline test still reported a verdict. Python (`_resolve_override`: exact key, then bare trailing segment) and Rust (`normalize_override_keys`: strip the single-model `<namespace>.` prefix) already honoured the local spelling. Julia is the reference binding: its `run_pde_tests` minted golden/ic_param_override.json. A second, RANK-3 (lon/lat/lev) pair generalises the category along the two axes a real model differs on: the `ic` is a separable coordinate expression over three index sets rather than one, and the pair is a CONTROLLED defaults-vs-overrides comparison -- `ic_param_override_rank3` carries the amplitude as an inline test's `parameter_overrides` while `ic_param_default_rank3` carries the same value as the parameter's declared `default`, and the two share one golden. That equality is what a hand-run control on a production model checks, promoted to a gate: a binding that drops an ic-only override from the build-time scope passes the default half and fails the override half.",
    "reference_binding": "julia",
    "bindings_required": [
        "julia",
        "python",
        "rust"
    ],
    "scope_excluded": {
        "go": "rewrite-only port; no makearray lowering / simulator / inline PDE-test runner",
        "typescript": "rewrite-only port; no makearray lowering / simulator / inline PDE-test runner"
    },
    "integrators": {
        "julia": {
            "algorithm": "Tsit5",
            "reltol": 1e-12,
            "abstol": 1e-14
        },
        "python": {
            "method": "RK45",
            "rtol": 1e-12,
            "atol": 1e-14
        },
        "rust": {
            "solver": "Erk",
            "reltol": 1e-12,
            "abstol": 1e-14
        }
    },
    "tolerances": {
        "assertion_rtol": 1e-09,
        "assertion_atol": 1e-11
    },
